  "_notes": [
    "archive_path values are literal on-disk paths under the container mount /archive (host: /mnt/data/regulatory_archive). Do not normalise the hyphen/underscore inconsistency in ICH dir names — match disk exactly.",
    "download_url is the direct fetch target used only when the source file is missing. source_url is provenance shown in the UI AND the fetch URL used by the ingestion pipeline — for ICH docs it must match download_url (direct PDF) since the ich.org landing pages are JS-rendered and produce no usable content after cleaning.",
    "CAVEAT 21-CFR-Part-11: download_url is the eCFR XML API endpoint, but the on-disk file is source.pdf. Download-if-missing is safe for the existing archive (file present, skip). For a genuine fresh install this entry needs a verified PDF source or an XML-handling path before its download can be trusted. Flagged, not resolved.",
    "title feeds both metadata_json.document_title and metadata_json.title (no dedicated title column in document_registry).",
    "document_class normalised to regulatory-public for all 9 (ICH-Q9-R1 was 'regulatory' in DB — corrected here as the authoritative source)."
  ],
